      "point": 13,
      "note": "Godan verbs may have a contracted causative-passive: 読む→読ませられる／読まされる. Ichidan 食べる stays 食べさせられる; する becomes させられる."
    },
    {
      "point": 20,
      "note": "The pattern is ～られてしまう (しまう), not ～られてしまる."
    },
    {
      "point": 31,
      "note": "The examples 読んどく／調べとく are contractions of ておく, not ていく."
    },
    {
      "point": 34,
      "note": "Use ～たりして for the light guess (e.g. 高かったりして); the formation is not simply ‘past form + りして’."
    },
    {
      "point": 48,
      "note": "Clause-linking examples like 実施し、まとめる use the ます-stem/連用形, not the て-form."
    },
    {
      "point": 103,
      "note": "The standard form is ～っぱなし. It can describe a neglected state (e.g. leaving something on) or an action that continues, often with a negative nuance."
    }
  ],
